WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.985 --> 00:00:05.563
Welcome to another Stories From The
Stores

00:00:05.568 --> 00:00:08.052
now today I'm joined by curator Donata Miller

00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:12.922
and she says it's time to show me something very interesting, so Donata what's this?

00:00:13.182 --> 00:00:15.727
This is a Chinese powdered incense clock.

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:19.194
It's a clock that uses
incense and fire to tell the time.

00:00:19.374 --> 00:00:24.805
It's from the 1700s onwards. Initially
incense clocks would be used in temples

00:00:24.805 --> 00:00:30.235
to tell the time with festivals or
when certain ceremonies needs to take place.

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:34.484
Okay so with incense clocks they
all have this really cool symbol in the middle?

00:00:34.764 --> 00:00:37.670
So not all incense clocks have this symbol,

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:42.880
but the modern incense clocks would often have a symbol of luck or goodwill in the middle.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.046
This is a character which is called 双喜 (shuāngxǐ)

00:00:46.227 --> 00:00:50.675
and it's a character which has been
translated to mean Double Happiness

00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:55.985
It's a character which is often used
in Chinese culture and often related to marriage.

00:00:55.985 --> 00:01:00.274
Something that scholars would
often use to feel inspired,

00:01:00.274 --> 00:01:07.067
smoke would come through the grates and it would trigger their emotions and imaginations.

00:01:07.348 --> 00:01:09.792
Okay so you've talked about how it works, can you show me?

00:01:10.093 --> 00:01:15.022
This clock has two different levels here and it shows us a little maze inside.

00:01:15.563 --> 00:01:19.772
We have these mazes, there's one that's more simple and one that's more complex

00:01:20.293 --> 00:01:22.777
These mazes would tell different amounts of time.

00:01:23.319 --> 00:01:26.064
You would use white words ash or you could also

00:01:26.074 --> 00:01:32.987
use powdered incense to lay a layer on
the tray and then press the maze imprint

00:01:32.987 --> 00:01:38.829
into this white wood ash and that
would leave a trail for you to light and measure the time that it is.

00:01:39.209 --> 00:01:41.614
Okay so you watch it, just watch it burn is what you do?

00:01:41.614 --> 00:01:45.281
You can watch it burn but you can
smell it burning also.

00:01:45.281 --> 00:01:48.908
Depending on the material that you've put inside, you'd be able to smell it.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:53.576
So what you're telling me is I could just know it's
11:15 because the room smells like roses?

00:01:53.576 --> 00:01:55.641
Basically yes!

00:01:55.641 --> 00:01:58.647
So why do you think it's so important that the museum has something like this?

00:01:59.168 --> 00:02:02.815
I think it shows a type of time measurement that we're not used to seeing

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:06.883
and it really shows that
Western culture doesn't own time

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:10.620
and that people from different cultures
and different societies have been

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:14.939
telling time in many different ways for
a very very long time.

